Goal

Reduce Cathedral’s actual LLM COGS when users perform multiple generations against the same project/context.

Important business rule: cache savings belong to Cathedral. Do not reduce the customer’s generation charge because a provider cache hit occurred.

Customer billing should continue using Cathedral’s normal published input/output rates.

Internally, separately track the true provider cost using:

* normal input tokens
* cached-read input tokens
* cache-write input tokens
* output tokens
* tool costs

This lets caching increase Cathedral’s margin without changing user-facing pricing.

