Avoid storing giant cached prompts in Supabase. The model provider owns the transient cache.

Required tests

At minimum plan tests proving:

1. Same unchanged project produces byte-identical stable prefixes.
2. Changing terminal beat does not alter the stable prefix.
3. Changing previous output does not alter the stable prefix.
4. Changing project/character data does alter the stable prefix.
5. Request IDs/timestamps never enter cached content.
6. Supported OpenAI request receives the intended cache key/breakpoint.
7. Unsupported models/providers still generate normally.
8. Total/cached/cache-write input token accounting cannot double-count.
9. Customer charge is unchanged whether the provider reports a cache hit or miss.
10. Actual provider COGS decreases on cache hits.
11. Preflight assumes no cache hit.
12. Existing generation persistence, credits, output sync, and error behavior remain intact.

